Q. How Kubenetes is different from Docker or any other container platform?
Ans: *Single Host  - Container's are Ephemeral means Short Lived. Container's are dependent on Single Host and for example if one 
Container is using more memory it impacts and kills other container which is short of memory resources running on Single Host. 
* Auto-Healling - Docker does'nt support Auto-Healling feature means if one container whichs is running the application gets
killed it doesn't automatically comes up. It's need to be started manually by someone from team like Devops Enginner. 
* Auto-Scalling and Load Balancing - Docker doen's support both Auto-Scalling and Load Balancing feature.
* Enterprise Support Solutions - Docker is a simple platform. It doesn't support any Enterprice Solutions like Load Balncer, Firewall, 
Auto-Scale, Healing, API-Gateways, blacklist and whitlist. 

Q. Advantages of Kubenetes over other container platform like Docker?
Ans: *Cluster Archetecture - Kubenetes suport Cluster means it have master and node archetecutre. So, if there are any faulty pods
which are impacting the application Kubenetes can immediately put that faulty pod in another node. 
* Auto-Scalling - Kubenetes have replication sets which uses YAML file from Deployment where you can define how may pods needs to be 
deployed and  Kubenetes have feature like HPA (Horizontal Pod AutoScalling) which automatically scales pods by using Metrics-API 
to read the metrics and autoscale pods. 
* Auto-Healing - If there is some issue with the Pods and it is about to be killed by using API Server Kubenetes imedditely responds
and roll-out a new pod. 
* Enterprise Support Solutions - It supports Enterprice Solutions like Load Balncer, Firewall, 
Auto-Scale, Healing, API-Gateways, blacklist and whitlist.
